{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 30, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind Adventure in Japan**\n\nLast month, I traded city chaos for Japan’s enchanting blend of tradition and futurism. My journey began in Tokyo, where neon lights flickered against the backdrop of towering skyscrapers. A quick stop at **Shibuya Crossing**—the world’s busiest pedestrian scramble—was both exhilarating and overwhelming. Later, I wandered through **Meiji Shrine**, a serene escape with towering cedar trees and peaceful gardens.\n\nThe next day, I boarded the **Shinkansen (bullet train)** to Kyoto, arriving in under two hours. Kyoto felt like stepping into a postcard: **Fushimi Inari Shrine**’s endless torii gates, the golden **Kinkaku-ji**, and the delicate beauty of **Arashiyama’s bamboo forest**. Tea ceremonies and kaiseki meals made me appreciate Japan’s meticulous craftsmanship.\n\nFrom Kyoto, I slipped into **Osaka**, where street food in **Dotonbori**—takoyaki, okonomiyaki, and ramens—was a feast for the senses. The **Osaka Castle** grounds offered a breath of fresh air, and the night views from **Umeda Sky Building** were breathtaking.\n\nMy final stop was **Hiroshima**, a moving reminder of history at the **Peace Memorial Park**. The **Miyajima Island** visit, with its iconic floating **Itsukushima Shrine**, was magical—especially during sunset.\n\nJapan’s efficiency, warmth, and contrast (old vs. new) left me inspired. Whether it was sipping matcha in a Kyoto teahouse or getting lost in Tokyo’s labyrinthine alleys, every moment was unforgettable. I’ll be back soon!", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.06550939381122589}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.27843376994132996}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.037113383412361145}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.018043426796793938}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": -4.7801782784517854e-05}, {"token": " Adventure", "logprob": -0.8805687427520752}, {"token": " in", "logpr